      "path": "src/ui/backup/test-support.ts",
      "content": "A configured responder that throws is evaluated before `Promise.resolve`, so the facade call throws synchronously instead of returning a rejected promise. Consequently, failure-path tests using `facade.exportBackup(request).catch(...)` (or rejection assertions) will bypass their promise error handling. Make the returned operation `async`, or catch responder exceptions and return `Promise.reject(error)`, so configured failures consistently use the promise-returning API.",
